teacher-jim-placeholder.jpg","about-015":"Jon Best","about-016":"/images/founding-teacher-jon-placeholder.jpg","about-017":"Education Affairs","about-018":"Oversees student recruitment and monitors teaching and learning activities.","about-019":"Minh Tam","about-020":"/images/team-nhat-linh-placeholder.jpg","about-021":"Nhat Linh","about-022":"/images/team-nhat-linh-placeholder.jpg","about-023":"Tu Thu","about-024":"/images/team-tu-thu-placeholder.jpg","about-025":"Hong Thu","about-026":"/images/team-hong-thu-placeholder.jpg","about-027":"Thu Trang","about-028":"/images/team-thu-trang-placeholder.jpg","about-029":"Human Resources","about-030":"Coordinates volunteer and team recruitment, and creates opportunities for the community to connect.","about-031":"Quynh Nhu","about-032":"/images/team-hr-placeholder.jpg","about-033":"Tra My","about-034":"/images/team-tra-my-placeholder.jpg","about-035":"Hong Hanh","about-036":"/images/team-hong-hanh-placeholder.jpg","about-037":"Ngoc Giau","about-038":"/images/team-ngoc-giau-placeholder.jpg","about-039":"Communication and Outreach","about-040":"Manages media channels, partnerships, and fundraising outreach.","about-041":"Quang Vinh","about-042":"/images/founding-teacher-jim-placeholder.jpg","about-043":"Hong Nhung","about-044":"/images/team-hong-nhung-placeholder.jpg","about-045":"Thao Ngan","about-046":"/images/team-thao-ngan-placeholder.jpg","about-047":"My Huyen","about-048":"/images/team-my-huyen-placeholder.jpg","about-049":"Thuy Tien","about-050":"/images/team-thuy-tien-placeholder.jpg","about-051":"About ABVN","about-052":"Better English.","about-053":"Better Future.","about-054":"A Better Vietnam is a non-profit project founded in 2017. We support young Vietnamese people, especially those in underprivileged areas, through free one-to-one online English lessons with volunteer native-speaking teachers.","about-055":"#our-story","about-056":"Our story","about-057":"#our-programme","about-058":"Our programme","about-059":"#our-values","about-060":"Our values","about-061":"#our-people","about-062":"Our people","about-063":"/images/learning-community.jpg","about-064":"Students learning and sharing ideas together","about-065":"Our story","about-066":"Opportunity should not depend on where you begin.","about-067":"In many parts of Vietnam, talented and motivated young people are held back not by a lack of ambition, but by a lack of opportunity. Limited access to quality English education and global connections can become barriers to further study, employment, and personal growth.","about-068":"A Better Vietnam was created to help bridge that gap. What began as a small initiative connecting Vietnamese students with volunteer English speakers has grown into a global, youth-led community for learning, exchange, and growth.","about-069":"At its heart, ABVN is about more than English. It is about helping young people gain confidence, find their voice, and discover opportunities beyond their immediate environment.","about-070":"/images/english-classroom.jpg","about-071":"Students taking part in an English class","about-072":"Our mission","about-073":"Help young people shape their own futures.","about-074":"We empower underprivileged Vietnamese students and young people through access to free English education and meaningful global connections.","about-075":"01","about-076":"Strengthen English communication skills.","about-077":"02","about-078":"Broaden global perspectives through language and cultural exchange.","about-079":"03","about-080":"Create opportunities for personal, academic, and professional development.","about-081":"With the right tools and support, young people can shape their futures and contribute positively to their communities.","about-082":"Our people","about-083":"A shared purpose. A dedicated community.","about-084":"Meet the founder, founding teachers, and teams who help bring ABVN’s mission to life.","about-085":"Meet the founder","about-086":"The idea that started A Better Vietnam.","about-087":"Mai Thi Thao Chi ","about-088":"· Founder","about-089":"A Better Vietnam was founded by Ms. Mai Thi Thao Chi, whose vision was to create equal access to English education for Vietnamese students, especially those from underprivileged backgrounds. Her leadership helped build a platform that supports English skills, confidence, connection, and personal growth.","about-090":"/images/founder-placeholder.jpg","about-091":"","about-092":"The people who built the foundation","about-093":"Meet our founding teachers.","about-094":"ABVN began with a small group of volunteer teachers who believed in the mission and supported the project from day one. Their dedication continues to inspire new generations of volunteers.","about-095":"","about-096":"Founding volunteer teacher","about-097":"People behind the work","about-098":"Meet our teams.","about-099":"ABVN’s teams coordinate learner support, volunteer recruitment, and outreach.","about-100":"","about-101":"Team Leader","about-102":"Team members","about-103":"","about-104":"/teachers","about-105":"Explore our teacher community ","about-106":"→","about-107":"What we do","about-108":"One-to-one learning, shaped by people.","about-109":"Through our online platform, teachers set their own schedules while learners book free lessons that fit their needs.","about-110":"For learners","about-111":"We provide free one-to-one online English lessons for motivated Vietnamese learners from underprivileged backgrounds. Learners are selected through an application and interview process. Once accepted, they can register for up to two lessons a week with different volunteer tutors during a six-month learning period.","about-112":"/student-apply","about-113":"Student program information","about-114":"For volunteer teachers","about-115":"Volunteers can teach from anywhere, set their own schedules, and choose methods that suit their students. After an application and interview process, teachers help learners develop English skills while sharing meaningful cross-cultural connections. Volunteering with ABVN is unpaid.","about-116":"/apply","about-117":"Volunteer teacher information","about-118":"Our values","about-119":"How we work together.","about-120":"Our journey","about-121":"From a few lessons to a global community.","about-122":"Each milestone reflects the people, partnerships, and shared commitment behind ABVN’s growth.","about-123":"Our impact and commitments","about-124":"Education that builds connection and opportunity.","about-125":"ABVN aligns its work with the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals and works to create a safe, respectful, and inclusive environment.","about-126":"Our commitments to the community","about-127":"✓","about-128":"Be part of the journey","about-129":"Help make English learning more accessible.","about-130":"Share your experience as a volunteer teacher or learn more about joining the student program.","about-131":"Interested in partnering with us?","about-132":"mailto:abettervnproject@gmail.com","about-133":"Contact ABVN","about-134":"/apply","about-135":"Become a teacher","about-136":"/student-apply","about-137":"Student program","journey-001":"2017","journey-002":"A small beginning","journey-003":"ABVN started with three volunteer teachers and a shared belief that small actions can create lasting change.","journey-004":"/images/volunteer-team.jpg","journey-005":"Volunteers coming together to support a shared mission","journey-006":"The first lessons","journey-007":"2019","journey-008":"Growing together","journey-009":"The program grew to 10 teachers, 170 students, and more than 2,300 lessons.","journey-010":"/images/english-classroom.jpg","journey-011":"Students taking part in a classroom lesson","journey-012":"10 teachers · 170 students","journey-013":"2020","journey-014":"Regional recognition","journey-015":"ABVN was selected as one of 20 Southeast Asian projects for the YSEALI Seeds for the Future program.","journey-016":"/images/learning-community.jpg","journey-017":"Learners sharing ideas and studying together","journey-018":"YSEALI Seeds for the Future","journey-019":"2021","journey-020":"Reaching more learners","journey-021":"With 35 teachers, the program expanded to include students in Laos and Cambodia.","journey-022":"/images/global-learning.jpg","journey-023":"People learning and collaborating across cultures","journey-024":"Vietnam · Laos · Cambodia","journey-025":"2024","journey-026":"An international community","journey-027":"The network had grown to more than 100 volunteer teachers, 1,000 students, and 25,000 lessons.","journey-028":"/images/student-community.jpg","journey-029":"A group of students learning and growing together","journey-030":"100+ teachers · 1,000+ learners","journey-031":"Select a year to explore a milestone in ABVN’s journey.","goals-001":"04","goals-002":"QUALITY EDUCATION","goals-003":"Quality education","goals-004":"Free one-to-one English lessons help learners access education that supports communication and lifelong learning.","goals-005":"ABVN’s core program pairs motivated Vietnamese learners with volunteer teachers for online English lessons.","goals-006":"/images/english-classroom.jpg","goals-007":"A student learning in a classroom","goals-008":"10","goals-009":"REDUCED INEQUALITIES","goals-010":"Reduced inequalities","goals-011":"The project focuses on learners who may face barriers to quality English education and global connections.","goals-012":"By making lessons free and accessible online, ABVN works to reduce barriers to learning opportunities.","goals-013":"/images/student-community.jpg","goals-014":"Students supporting one another in a learning community","goals-015":"17","goals-016":"PARTNERSHIPS FOR THE GOALS","goals-017":"Partnerships for the goals","goals-018":"Volunteer teachers and collaborators from different places work together to support young people.","goals-019":"ABVN’s international network connects educators, learners, and partners around a shared purpose.","goals-020":"/images/global-learning.jpg","goals-021":"People working together as a global community","goals-022":"SDG ","goals-023":"→","goals-024":"Sustainable Development Goal "},"sections":["about-section-1","about-section-2","about-section-3","about-section-4","about-section-5","about-section-6","about-section-7"]}'::jsonb);
insert into public.content_templates(key,definition) values ('news','{}'::jsonb);
insert into public.content_documents(key,draft,published) values ('news','{"articles":[{"slug":"autumn-2026-volunteer-teachers-welcome","title":"Welcome to our autumn 2026 volunteer teacher cohort","category":"Community","date":"2026-10-12","summary":"Twenty-four new volunteer teachers from nine countries have joined ABVN this term, ready to start weekly conversation sessions with students across Vietnam.","image":"/images/volunteer-team.jpg","body":["This term, 24 volunteer teachers from nine countries are joining A Better Vietnam’s learning community. They bring a range of experiences and a shared interest in helping students build confidence using English.","Teachers and learners meet for weekly conversation sessions. Together, they practise speaking, explore new topics, and learn about each other’s cultures in a friendly online setting.","We’re delighted to welcome the new cohort and grateful to everyone who gives their time to make these connections possible. We look forward to sharing more stories from their sessions throughout the term."],"imageAlt":"Welcome to our autumn 2026 volunteer teacher cohort","status":"published"},{"slug":"student-speaking-showcase-hanoi","title":"Students shine at the ABVN speaking showcase","category":"Events","date":"2026-09-27","summary":"More than 80 learners presented short talks on technology, travel, and local traditions in a day of confident, creative English.","image":"/images/student-community.jpg","body":["More than 80 learners took part in the ABVN speaking showcase, sharing short presentations on topics that matter to them. Technology, travel, and local traditions all featured in a lively programme.","The showcase gave students an opportunity to practise organizing their ideas, speaking to an audience, and listening to one another. Each presentation reflected the learner’s own interests and perspective.","Thank you to the students, volunteers, and organizers who made the event possible. We’re proud of everyone who stepped up to speak and support their fellow learners."],"imageAlt":"Students shine at the ABVN speaking showcase","status":"published"},{"slug":"new-partner-schools-central-highlands","title":"Five new partner schools join the network","category":"Partnerships","date":"2026-09-10","summary":"ABVN is expanding its reach to the Central Highlands, bringing free English practice to students who have had limited access to native-speaking teachers.","image":"/images/learning-community.jpg","body":["Five partner schools in the Central Highlands have joined the A Better Vietnam network. This collaboration is an opportunity to connect more students with regular English conversation practice.","Through online sessions with volunteer teachers, learners can practise speaking in a supportive setting and discover new perspectives through conversation. Schools help connect students with the programme and provide local support.","We’re grateful to our new school partners for working with us to make learning opportunities more accessible. We hope this is the beginning of a lasting collaboration."],"imageAlt":"Five new partner schools join the network","status":"published"},{"slug":"10000-sessions-milestone","title":"A milestone: 10,000 sessions taught this year","category":"Milestones","date":"2026-08-21","summary":"Thanks to our volunteers, ABVN reached 10,000 live learning sessions in 2026, a new record for the community.","image":"/images/global-learning.jpg","body":["A Better Vietnam has reached 10,000 live learning sessions in 2026. This milestone reflects the time and care volunteers have shared with learners throughout the year.","Every session is a chance to practise English, ask questions, and build the confidence to communicate. Behind the total are many individual conversations and the relationships that grow over time.","Thank you to all our volunteer teachers, students, and partners for making this possible. We’ll keep working to create welcoming spaces for learners to practise and connect."],"imageAlt":"A milestone: 10,000 sessions taught this year","status":"published"},{"slug":"summer-english-camp-recap","title":"Summer English camp recap: stories, songs, and new friends","category":"Events","date":"2026-07-30","summary":"Two weeks of games, storytelling, and cultural exchange wrapped up with a closing ceremony attended by families and volunteers online.","image":"/images/english-classroom.jpg","body":["ABVN’s summer English camp brought students together for two weeks of activities built around communication and creativity. Games and storytelling offered plenty of chances to use English in a relaxed way.","Learners also shared traditions and stories from their own lives, making cultural exchange part of the experience. Volunteers joined online to encourage students and take part in the activities.","The camp ended with a virtual celebration for students, families, and volunteers. Thank you to everyone who helped make these weeks memorable."],"imageAlt":"Summer English camp recap: stories, songs, and new friends","status":"published"},{"slug":"volunteer-training-workshop-series","title":"Volunteer training workshop series now open","category":"Volunteering","date":"2026-07-08","summary":"A new series of free online workshops helps teachers prepare for engaging, learner-friendly conversation sessions.","image":"/images/volunteer-team.jpg","body":["ABVN is opening a new series of free online workshops for volunteer teachers. The sessions are designed to help volunteers prepare conversation activities that are engaging and welcoming for learners.","Workshop topics include planning a session around student interests, encouraging participation, and adapting activities for different levels of confidence. Teachers can share ideas and learn from one another.","The workshops are part of ABVN’s ongoing support for volunteers. We believe that thoughtful preparation helps create positive learning experiences for everyone in the conversation."],"imageAlt":"Volunteer training workshop series now open","status":"published"},{"slug":"student-scholarship-announcement","title":"Learning grants announced for 2026–2027 students","category":"Announcements","date":"2026-06-18","summary":"ABVN has opened applications for learning grants that help motivated students get the devices and connectivity they need to join sessions.","image":"/images/student-community.jpg","body":["Applications are open for ABVN learning grants for the 2026–2027 school year. The grants are intended to help students access the equipment or internet connectivity they need to take part in online learning sessions.","Reliable access to a device and connection can make it easier for learners to join regular sessions and stay connected with their teachers. The programme aims to reduce some of the practical barriers students may face.","Students interested in applying can contact the ABVN team for information about eligibility and the application process. We look forward to supporting learners as they continue their studies."],"imageAlt":"Learning grants announced for 2026–2027 students","status":"published"},{"slug":"teacher-spotlight-cultural-exchange","title":"Teacher spotlight: sharing culture through conversation","category":"Community","date":"2026-05-29","summary":"Our founding teachers reflect on the friendships and surprises that come from years of weekly sessions with Vietnamese learners.","image":"/images/founding-teachers-placeholder.jpg","body":["For ABVN’s founding teachers, the most memorable part of volunteering is often the conversation itself. Week after week, teachers and learners get to know one another while practising English together.","Sessions can lead to unexpected discoveries: a shared interest, a new point of view, or a story about everyday life in another country. These moments make language practice feel personal and bring cultures closer.","We’re thankful to the teachers who helped shape ABVN’s community and continue to share their time with learners. Their commitment shows how meaningful a regular conversation can be."],"imageAlt":"Teacher spotlight: sharing culture through conversation","status":"published"},{"slug":"sdg-education-week","title":"Celebrating education for all during SDG Education Week","category":"Impact","date":"2026-05-05","summary":"ABVN joined the global conversation on quality education, sharing how free, volunteer-led English practice supports young people.","image":"/images/global-learning.jpg","body":["During SDG Education Week, A Better Vietnam joined educators and communities reflecting on the importance of inclusive, quality learning opportunities.","ABVN’s volunteer-led English sessions give students a place to practise communication and connect with teachers from around the world. Regular conversation complements classroom learning and encourages learners to use their skills with confidence.","We’re proud to be part of a community working toward wider access to education. Thank you to our students, volunteers, and partners for contributing to that shared effort."],"imageAlt":"Celebrating education for all during SDG Education Week","status":"published"}]}'::jsonb,'{"articles":[{"slug":"autumn-2026-volunteer-teachers-welcome","title":"Welcome to our autumn 2026 volunteer teacher cohort","category":"Community","date":"2026-10-12","summary":"Twenty-four new volunteer teachers from nine countries have joined ABVN this term, ready to start weekly conversation sessions with students across Vietnam.","image":"/images/volunteer-team.jpg","body":["This term, 24 volunteer teachers from nine countries are joining A Better Vietnam’s learning community. They bring a range of experiences and a shared interest in helping students build confidence using English.","Teachers and learners meet for weekly conversation sessions. Together, they practise speaking, explore new topics, and learn about each other’s cultures in a friendly online setting.","We’re delighted to welcome the new cohort and grateful to everyone who gives their time to make these connections possible. We look forward to sharing more stories from their sessions throughout the term."],"imageAlt":"Welcome to our autumn 2026 volunteer teacher cohort","status":"published"},{"slug":"student-speaking-showcase-hanoi","title":"Students shine at the ABVN speaking showcase","category":"Events","date":"2026-09-27","summary":"More than 80 learners presented short talks on technology, travel, and local traditions in a day of confident, creative English.","image":"/images/student-community.jpg","body":["More than 80 learners took part in the ABVN speaking showcase, sharing short presentations on topics that matter to them. Technology, travel, and local traditions all featured in a lively programme.","The showcase gave students an opportunity to practise organizing their ideas, speaking to an audience, and listening to one another. Each presentation reflected the learner’s own interests and perspective.","Thank you to the students, volunteers, and organizers who made the event possible. We’re proud of everyone who stepped up to speak and support their fellow learners."],"imageAlt":"Students shine at the ABVN speaking showcase","status":"published"},{"slug":"new-partner-schools-central-highlands","title":"Five new partner schools join the network","category":"Partnerships","date":"2026-09-10","summary":"ABVN is expanding its reach to the Central Highlands, bringing free English practice to students who have had limited access to native-speaking teachers.","image":"/images/learning-community.jpg","body":["Five partner schools in the Central Highlands have joined the A Better Vietnam network. This collaboration is an opportunity to connect more students with regular English conversation practice.","Through online sessions with volunteer teachers, learners can practise speaking in a supportive setting and discover new perspectives through conversation. Schools help connect students with the programme and provide local support.","We’re grateful to our new school partners for working with us to make learning opportunities more accessible. We hope this is the beginning of a lasting collaboration."],"imageAlt":"Five new partner schools join the network","status":"published"},{"slug":"10000-sessions-milestone","title":"A milestone: 10,000 sessions taught this year","category":"Milestones","date":"2026-08-21","summary":"Thanks to our volunteers, ABVN reached 10,000 live learning sessions in 2026, a new record for the community.","image":"/images/global-learning.jpg","body":["A Better Vietnam has reached 10,000 live learning sessions in 2026. This milestone reflects the time and care volunteers have shared with learners throughout the year.","Every session is a chance to practise English, ask questions, and build the confidence to communicate. Behind the total are many individual conversations and the relationships that grow over time.","Thank you to all our volunteer teachers, students, and partners for making this possible. We’ll keep working to create welcoming spaces for learners to practise and connect."],"imageAlt":"A milestone: 10,000 sessions taught this year","status":"published"},{"slug":"summer-english-camp-recap","title":"Summer English camp recap: stories, songs, and new friends","category":"Events","date":"2026-07-30","summary":"Two weeks of games, storytelling, and cultural exchange wrapped up with a closing ceremony attended by families and volunteers online.","image":"/images/english-classroom.jpg","body":["ABVN’s summer English camp brought students together for two weeks of activities built around communication and creativity. Games and storytelling offered plenty of chances to use English in a relaxed way.","Learners also shared traditions and stories from their own lives, making cultural exchange part of the experience. Volunteers joined online to encourage students and take part in the activities.","The camp ended with a virtual celebration for students, families, and volunteers. Thank you to everyone who helped make these weeks memorable."],"imageAlt":"Summer English camp recap: stories, songs, and new friends","status":"published"},{"slug":"volunteer-training-workshop-series","title":"Volunteer training workshop series now open","category":"Volunteering","date":"2026-07-08","summary":"A new series of free online workshops helps teachers prepare for engaging, learner-friendly conversation sessions.","image":"/images/volunteer-team.jpg","body":["ABVN is opening a new series of free online workshops for volunteer teachers. The sessions are designed to help volunteers prepare conversation activities that are engaging and welcoming for learners.","Workshop topics include planning a session around student interests, encouraging participation, and adapting activities for different levels of confidence. Teachers can share ideas and learn from one another.","The workshops are part of ABVN’s ongoing support for volunteers. We believe that thoughtful preparation helps create positive learning experiences for everyone in the conversation."],"imageAlt":"Volunteer training workshop series now open","status":"published"},{"slug":"student-scholarship-announcement","title":"Learning grants announced for 2026–2027 students","category":"Announcements","date":"2026-06-18","summary":"ABVN has opened applications for learning grants that help motivated students get the devices and connectivity they need to join sessions.","image":"/images/student-community.jpg","body":["Applications are open for ABVN learning grants for the 2026–2027 school year. The grants are intended to help students access the equipment or internet connectivity they need to take part in online learning sessions.","Reliable access to a device and connection can make it easier for learners to join regular sessions and stay connected with their teachers. The programme aims to reduce some of the practical barriers students may face.","Students interested in applying can contact the ABVN team for information about eligibility and the application process. We look forward to supporting learners as they continue their studies."],"imageAlt":"Learning grants announced for 2026–2027 students","status":"published"},{"slug":"teacher-spotlight-cultural-exchange","title":"Teacher spotlight: sharing culture through conversation","category":"Community","date":"2026-05-29","summary":"Our founding teachers reflect on the friendships and surprises that come from years of weekly sessions with Vietnamese learners.","image":"/images/founding-teachers-placeholder.jpg","body":["For ABVN’s founding teachers, the most memorable part of volunteering is often the conversation itself. Week after week, teachers and learners get to know one another while practising English together.","Sessions can lead to unexpected discoveries: a shared interest, a new point of view, or a story about everyday life in another country. These moments make language practice feel personal and bring cultures closer.","We’re thankful to the teachers who helped shape ABVN’s community and continue to share their time with learners. Their commitment shows how meaningful a regular conversation can be."],"imageAlt":"Teacher spotlight: sharing culture through conversation","status":"published"},{"slug":"sdg-education-week","title":"Celebrating education for all during SDG Education Week","category":"Impact","date":"2026-05-05","summary":"ABVN joined the global conversation on quality education, sharing how free, volunteer-led English practice supports young people.","image":"/images/global-learning.jpg","body":["During SDG Education Week, A Better Vietnam joined educators and communities reflecting on the importance of inclusive, quality learning opportunities.","ABVN’s volunteer-led English sessions give students a place to practise communication and connect with teachers from around the world. Regular conversation complements classroom learning and encourages learners to use their skills with confidence.","We’re proud to be part of a community working toward wider access to education. Thank you to our students, volunteers, and partners for contributing to that shared effort."],"imageAlt":"Celebrating education for all during SDG Education Week","status":"published"}]}'::jsonb);
